1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,760
Jesus stopped reading
in the middle of a sentence.

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:05,540
In Nazareth, His home town,
He read God's promise

3
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:07,800
of someone sent with good news
for the poor,

4
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:10,030
and a time of God's welcome.

5
00:00:10,070 --> 00:00:12,420
The prophet Isaiah's sentence goes on:

6
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:15,360
"and the day of vengeance of our God."

7
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:19,000
He left the day of vengeance unread,
and sat down.

8
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:22,550
"This day is this scripture fulfilled."

9
00:00:22,590 --> 00:00:24,210
It was about Him.

10
00:00:24,610 --> 00:00:26,920
They would want miracles, and say:

11
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:29,460
"Physician, heal thyself."

12
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:34,680
He reminded them God once sent help
to foreigners, not to their own.

13
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:38,120
Furious, they took Him to a cliff
to throw Him down.

14
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,280
He walked right through them.

15
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:43,200
Later, at the cross, the same dare:

16
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:45,960
"He saved others; let him save himself."

17
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,260
This time, He stayed.

18
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:50,970
He died, and rose again.

19
00:00:51,010 --> 00:00:53,250
He stopped reading at the welcome.

20
00:00:53,650 --> 00:00:57,450
It is still open, for you, today.
